    "assessment": "Accepted as a measured retained-inventory and performance hotfix for this four-priest reconstruction. Exact Factorio 2.1.25 native headless comparison replayed the same original save with four reconstructed rank units on one runner job for 18,000 ticks; the first 600 ticks were excluded and callback instrumentation was disabled. Both versions retained all four moving identities and completed 35 acquisitions, 35 deposits and one emergency transaction. Whole-update mean improved from 18.6433 to 2.4337 ms, p95 from 188.8359 to 8.6968 ms and p99 from 377.2106 to 27.6365 ms. The candidate late-window mean was 2.4737 ms and p99 was 28.8316 ms. Residual stalls remain: 37 measured candidate updates exceeded 50 ms and one exceeded 100 ms, with a 107.5013 ms maximum. The bounded integration audit fully traversed 102,503 nodes using 674,784 work units and reached complete without truncation or unsupported values; lifecycle and registry audits completed. There were no isolated handler, service or native runtime errors. These are measured results for this mod stack and reconstruction, with passive observation present in both cases."
